From 35ab766b93c957fe8db77c8cf2cb84c89703be48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:18:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] extcon: sm5502: reset the chip once in the boot-time
 re-detection

The re-detection wrote the reset register and then called
sm5502_init_dev_type(), which starts with a reset of its own. The second
reset is still in progress when the configuration follows it, and the
CONTROL write that unmasks the interrupt output is lost: read back right
after, CONTROL is 0x00, and once the chip settles it is back at its
default 0x1f. From the re-detection on, about 19 s after boot, the MUIC
reported no attach or detach at all until the next boot.

Leave the reset to sm5502_init_dev_type(). A single reset followed by the
configuration holds, measured with the write from 0.35 ms after it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
 drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
index dc653eab18..1ae6cd4e21 100644
--- a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
+++ b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
@@ -768,8 +768,10 @@ static void sm5502_muic_detect_cable_wq(struct work_struct *work)
 	 * recorded as a plain SDP one.
 	 *
 	 * Reset the chip so it measures again, now that the host has had time
-	 * to enumerate, and put the configuration back afterwards: the reset
-	 * clears the interrupt masks along with everything else.
+	 * to enumerate. sm5502_init_dev_type() starts with the reset and then
+	 * puts the configuration back; a second reset just before it would
+	 * still be in progress when CONTROL is written, and the write that
+	 * unmasks the interrupt output would be lost.
 	 */
 	/*
 	 * The reset opens the USB switch for a moment and every USB session
@@ -788,7 +790,6 @@ static void sm5502_muic_detect_cable_wq(struct work_struct *work)
 		 * the USB switch in the middle of it.
 		 */
 		disable_irq(info->irq);
-		regmap_write(info->regmap, SM5502_REG_RESET, SM5502_REG_RESET_MASK);
 		sm5502_init_dev_type(info);
 
 		/*
